WEBVTT

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:28.970
Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!!

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:34.210
Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!!

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:39.050
Calling everything delicious!

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:43.550
The more I eat, the more powerful I get!

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:46.920
Let’s capture ingredients around the world!

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:51.500
I dream of being an invincible 
Gourmet Fighter!!

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:56.530
Now on to the bottom of the 
sea, or the tops of glaciers!

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:59.200
Jump! Jump Jump Jump! 
Knock! Knock Knock Knock!

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.400
Give thanks!

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:04.610
Let’s eat!

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:10.410
Wow wo!! Spiked Punch! Wow wo!! Multi-fold!

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:15.550
Guts! Gutsy Guts! I can eat any dream!

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:20.820
Wow wo!! My very own... 
Wow wo!! ...Full Course!

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:24.990
Guts! Gutsy Guts! Gather them all up!

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:31.070
And put the world on my plate!

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:33.870
Wow wow wow! Eat the mountains!!

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:36.440
Wow wow wow! Toriko!!

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:39.040
Wow wow wow! Eat the oceans!!

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:43.310
Wow wow wow! Tori, Tori, Tori, Toriko!!

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:50.420
Someone once said...

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:55.720
There are trees that have 
the deliciously rich

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:59.330
yet refreshing and mild 
taste of mayonnaise...

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:03.160
Mayonnaitrees!

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:08.270
There are dragonflies that 
are soft, taste mildly sweet,

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:11.040
melt in your mouth, and look 
like round egg cookies...

00:02:11.710 --> 00:02:14.910
Round Eggonflies!

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:18.680
The world is in the Gourmet Age...

00:02:19.210 --> 00:02:24.180
An age in which people quest for 
yet unknown culinary delights!

00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:29.420
Shaved Ice

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:38.030
Thank you for the food!

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:47.810
Freezin'!

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:51.310
Just like the name promises! 
It's surprisingly good!

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:58.280
Those Stun Apples we picked last time 
can be annoyingly sour sometimes.

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:00.750
Well, they look annoying, too...

00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:03.860
But when you put this Sherbet Apple on top,

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:08.190
it makes it pleasantly cool 
and balances the taste.

00:03:10.430 --> 00:03:12.530
It is good, isn't it?

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:15.200
It's also tasty with sweet red beans on top.

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:19.070
Shall we order something to drink?

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:19.600
Yeah!

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:22.210
You look like you're dying 
to quench your thirst

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:26.340
with a crisp chilled fruity 
liquor, Toriko-san.

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:28.050
You can tell, Komatsu?!

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:33.750
Excuse me! Apple brandy and soda 
and a glass of apple juice, please!

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:35.050
Now you're obsessed with apples?!

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:39.020
Although I do feel like sinkin' 
my teeth into apples these days...

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:42.730
But what the heck? You're 
being unusually considerate.

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:44.860
And you look like the cat 
that swallowed the canary!

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:47.160
You can tell?

00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:49.030
That expression is makin' me sick.

00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:50.830
What, did somethin' good happen to you?

00:03:51.070 --> 00:03:52.500
Yes, actually...

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:54.300
Thank you for your patience.

00:03:56.610 --> 00:03:58.740
What is it?! Spit it out!

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:02.450
Actually... I won!

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:04.820
Won? Won what?

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:08.250
In a word, the Gourmet Jumbo Lottery!

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:16.590
Chicken Beast's Egg! The Memories 
of Old Man Yocchi and His Wife!

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:22.570
The Gourmet Jumbo is

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:26.000
that generous lottery with a 10 
billion yen first prize, right?

00:04:26.470 --> 00:04:28.740
That's awesome, Komatsu!

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:31.070
Don't broadcast it!

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:35.640
Does this mean our trip to the 
Gourmet Shrine made you lucky?

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:40.050
Yeah, I guess my luck has taken 
a turn for the better since then.

00:04:40.150 --> 00:04:42.820
So how much did you win?

00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:46.090
Listen to this. But don't be too surprised!

00:04:46.190 --> 00:04:46.520
Okay!

00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:51.130
I won the 8th place prize, a million yen!

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:54.660
E-Eighth place?! That's low!

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:56.530
No, it isn't!

00:04:56.530 --> 00:05:00.270
Sure it is! Can you really 
call eighth place "good luck"?

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:02.270
You surprised me there!

00:05:02.270 --> 00:05:04.770
Hell, the Stun Apples would've 
been shocked by that!

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:09.580
Well... maybe eighth place 
is no big deal to you...

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:13.110
But a million yen is still a lot of money!

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:16.550
My hands were quivering when I got the cash!

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:18.720
Yeah, that's true.

00:05:18.890 --> 00:05:20.390
A million is a good chunk of change.

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:22.020
Use it wisely.

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:24.790
Um... So I was thinking...

00:05:25.690 --> 00:05:28.660
I want to treat you to something today,

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:32.530
as a way of saying thanks for everything.

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:34.800
What? You're gonna treat me?!

00:05:34.970 --> 00:05:41.580
Uh-huh. You're always paying my way, so 
when a windfall like this comes along,

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:43.140
the least I can do is...

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:43.710
Perfect timing!

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:45.980
Right now, there's somethin' I want!

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:50.380
Really?! Then let me get 
it for you as a present.

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:52.850
So what is this thing you want?

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:53.620
Land!

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:54.890
Land?!

00:05:55.420 --> 00:06:00.190
Yeah! And I was headin' over 
that way now, so this works out!

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:04.630
Th-That's impossible! You 
can't buy land for a million!

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:06.800
I guess you have a point...

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:11.770
Toriko-san... Since when have you 
been so interested in buying land?

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:15.510
You don't mean to live 
there yourself, do you?

00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:18.910
Just how much land do you need?

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:20.610
It's just a few square meters.

00:06:20.950 --> 00:06:23.180
A nice piece of land is up for sale.

00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:25.080
A few square meters?

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:28.720
Come to think of it, the other day...

00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:31.190
Gourmet News!

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:34.030
Our top story of the day is:

00:06:34.590 --> 00:06:39.260
The so-called "Enormous 
Plot" is up for public sale.

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:43.600
The lowest bid is ten billion yen.

00:06:48.570 --> 00:06:53.410
Don't tell me inside that giant 
duralumin case, you've got...

00:06:57.180 --> 00:06:59.580
A chicken that has the appearance of a tiger.

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:02.790
It's an Avian Beast, the Chicken Beast.

00:07:03.550 --> 00:07:07.390
The eggs this Beast lays are 
top of the line ingredients,

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:11.060
but the Chicken Beast refuses to lay any eggs

00:07:11.060 --> 00:07:12.630
other than in a spot that it likes.

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:18.030
And the spot that it likes is 
this little parcel of land.

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:22.470
Is that why the land is so expensive?

00:07:23.070 --> 00:07:25.740
The owner of the land is 
an old man named Yocchi,

00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:28.340
but he's a stubborn son of a gun.

00:07:28.950 --> 00:07:33.320
Up to now, any number of reputable 
gourmet land developers and rich people

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:38.450
have tried to buy the land from him, but 
he apparently refused to hear them out.

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:42.390
Word is that even IGO top brass 
weren't allowed on the property.

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:47.430
I wonder why he's willing to let 
that Enormous Plot go now...

00:07:47.630 --> 00:07:48.760
I dunno...

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:52.100
But I say we pay a visit to Old 
Man Yocchi and ask him ourselves.

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:57.410
There's 50 billion yen here.

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:03.950
Cheap! 50 billion is so 
cheap, I'm offended! Shoo!

00:08:04.010 --> 00:08:05.450
I can prepare more.

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:07.480
As much as you desire...

00:08:07.580 --> 00:08:09.450
Go away! And never come back!

00:08:09.650 --> 00:08:10.720
I don't want your billions!

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:13.390
Apparently, even 50 billion doesn't cut it.

00:08:13.690 --> 00:08:15.320
That greedy old bastard...

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:17.890
Nobody's gonna be able to bid at this rate!

00:08:19.090 --> 00:08:21.030
How high does he intend to jack the price?!

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:23.200
They're already at it.

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:26.270
Sure hope it hasn't been sold already...

00:08:35.810 --> 00:08:39.610
Chicken Beast (Avian Beast) Capture Level 50

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:39.380
Is that the Avian Beast... 
the Chicken Beast?!

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:48.960
It's huge!

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:54.460
Then that's the Enormous Plot, huh?

00:09:01.070 --> 00:09:03.200
I'm gonna forget about 
dealing with that old fart.

00:09:03.900 --> 00:09:07.070
All we gotta do is capture that Chicken 
Beast and I'll be a multibillionaire!

00:09:48.280 --> 00:09:50.280
Take it alive!

00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:52.250
Flying Fork!

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:04.600
One of the Four Kings, Toriko!

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:07.200
You shouldn't think about 
catching a Chicken Beast hen.

00:10:08.570 --> 00:10:13.940
When it's under stress from an enemy, 
it affects the eggs that it lays.

00:10:16.910 --> 00:10:19.740
Go back to your nest, Meeko!

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:21.110
Meeko?!

00:10:35.630 --> 00:10:37.590
You can take a load off in here.

00:10:42.430 --> 00:10:43.230
Let's go, Komatsu.

00:10:43.230 --> 00:10:44.470
Right.

00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:59.580
For someone who owns a huge tract 
of land, this is pretty austere...

00:11:00.120 --> 00:11:03.250
I imagined him living in a big mansion...

00:11:05.750 --> 00:11:06.890
Hello there.

00:11:08.660 --> 00:11:09.960
Thank you for inviting us in.

00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:11.690
This smell!

00:11:12.800 --> 00:11:16.430
So this is it?! The scent 
of a Chicken Beast's egg!

00:11:16.670 --> 00:11:19.170
You smell something, Toriko-san?

00:11:19.270 --> 00:11:23.000
Oh. You must have a good sense of smell.

00:11:23.670 --> 00:11:26.440
You're that Gourmet Hunter, 
Toriko, aren't you?

00:11:27.010 --> 00:11:30.210
Nice to meet you, Old Man Yocchi.

00:11:30.810 --> 00:11:34.880
I came here today to buy 
a bit of land, but now...

00:11:35.680 --> 00:11:37.890
I wanna eat an egg!

00:11:38.420 --> 00:11:42.520
I can't get enough of this sweet 
aroma that smells like candy!

00:11:46.930 --> 00:11:49.130
I want to eat an egg, too!

00:11:49.530 --> 00:11:50.100
Hmph!

00:11:51.070 --> 00:11:52.800
It's been a long time

00:11:52.800 --> 00:11:55.640
since somebody's wanted an egg 
just to satisfy their appetite.

00:11:57.040 --> 00:12:04.040
Those cretins outside only intend to 
use Meeko and her eggs to make money.

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:10.320
In this Gourmet Age, anybody who 
wants land is in it to make a profit.

00:12:13.390 --> 00:12:15.560
So, you want to try an egg?

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:18.430
That's a Chicken Beast's egg?!

00:12:21.490 --> 00:12:23.030
Thank you!

00:12:23.030 --> 00:12:25.330
U-Um, I'll help you cook it!

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:28.000
My name is Komatsu and I'm a chef.

00:12:28.470 --> 00:12:30.170
I'm partners with Toriko-san.

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:32.770
You're Toriko's partner, you say?

00:12:33.410 --> 00:12:35.680
Then I'll gladly accept your help!

00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:36.840
Great!

00:12:40.250 --> 00:12:41.410
Thank you for your patience!

00:12:42.680 --> 00:12:46.920
We made a fluffy plain omelet 
with just a Chicken Beast egg,

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:49.620
Garlic Chicken chawan-mushi,

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:53.390
and ginger pork and creamy 
matsutake mushroom egg chanpuru!

00:12:53.860 --> 00:12:56.190
Everything looks delicious!

00:12:57.030 --> 00:13:00.270
I give thanks for all of 
this world's bounty...

00:13:01.070 --> 00:13:02.530
Let's eat!

00:13:22.920 --> 00:13:26.090
It's mellow, but also with 
a strong, firm flavor!

00:13:35.800 --> 00:13:36.730
Old Man Yocchi...

00:13:37.030 --> 00:13:38.870
You used to be a Gourmet Hunter?

00:13:39.400 --> 00:13:43.210
Yeah, but I retired years and years ago.

00:13:43.870 --> 00:13:49.580
Are you the one who tamed the Chicken 
Beast and trained it to lay eggs?

00:13:50.080 --> 00:13:51.250
That's right.

00:13:52.220 --> 00:13:55.790
A long time ago, I found 
a baby chick over there...

00:13:57.750 --> 00:14:01.930
...and was surprised to see that it 
was actually a Chicken Beast chick!

00:14:02.460 --> 00:14:04.090
You raised it from a chick?!

00:14:04.790 --> 00:14:09.570
Adult Chicken Beasts are violent 
with a capture level of at least 50.

00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:11.330
They're extremely dangerous.

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:15.500
That's exactly why no one 
can just swipe the eggs

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:18.140
from that three square meter space.

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:22.980
What made you decide to raise 
a violent chick like that?

00:14:23.410 --> 00:14:24.480
For the money?

00:14:24.610 --> 00:14:26.820
No! Watch your mouth!

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:38.190
The year prior to that, my wife passed away.

00:14:40.060 --> 00:14:43.830
I was still a Gourmet Hunter then...

00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:48.870
At the time, I worked like a madman.

00:14:49.370 --> 00:14:56.240
My wife had always been sick, 
and so, to make her stronger,

00:14:56.610 --> 00:14:58.680
I worked hard to be able to 
feed her the finest foods.

00:14:59.010 --> 00:15:03.320
I took on all jobs and devoted myself 
to searching for ingredients, but...

00:15:04.220 --> 00:15:05.720
Hey! I'm home!

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:10.060
My wife's illness had taken 
a turn for the worse...

00:15:10.660 --> 00:15:12.260
By the time I'd finished the job

00:15:12.260 --> 00:15:14.930
and gotten home for the first 
time in a long while...

00:15:15.330 --> 00:15:16.960
...it was too late.

00:15:17.930 --> 00:15:21.870
I'll never forget her 
last words to me then...

00:15:22.700 --> 00:15:26.340
You sent home more money 
than I could ever spend...

00:15:27.710 --> 00:15:33.910
But I would have traded it all to just 
have even one more meal together...

00:15:41.790 --> 00:15:42.520
What...

00:15:44.860 --> 00:15:46.990
What was I doing?

00:15:48.530 --> 00:15:50.260
Just chasing after money...

00:15:51.100 --> 00:15:53.830
I'm... a terrible husband.

00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:59.840
Being a Gourmet Hunter is a 
means, not an end in itself.

00:16:01.210 --> 00:16:06.140
You'd forgotten that the most 
important thing is to enjoy a meal.

00:16:06.850 --> 00:16:15.150
Pathetically, I could remember only 
one of my wife's favorite foods.

00:16:16.350 --> 00:16:19.320
That was the egg of a Chicken Beast.

00:16:19.760 --> 00:16:23.090
She always looked so happy eating it...

00:16:24.630 --> 00:16:29.270
When I discovered the Chicken Beast 
chick, I thought it was fate.

00:16:30.230 --> 00:16:31.440
You see, the reason is...

00:16:32.200 --> 00:16:37.070
...that's the place where my wife 
and I first shared a meal together.

00:16:37.610 --> 00:16:38.240
And not only that...

00:16:42.910 --> 00:16:46.020
It's mellow, yet has a strong, firm taste.

00:16:46.480 --> 00:16:48.090
This is so delicious...

00:16:49.350 --> 00:16:53.020
We ate a Chicken Beast egg together then.

00:16:56.130 --> 00:16:58.660
I carried that memory with me,

00:16:59.300 --> 00:17:03.370
so I got it into my head that 
the chick was my wife reborn.

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:07.340
My wife's name was Miko.

00:17:08.070 --> 00:17:12.080
I named the chick Meeko 
and decided to raise her.

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:15.140
This time, I swore...

00:17:15.140 --> 00:17:18.610
I swore I'd cherish her and never 
leave, even for a moment...

00:17:21.380 --> 00:17:24.050
That was over 50 years ago...

00:17:24.790 --> 00:17:27.220
I retired from being a Gourmet Hunter

00:17:27.220 --> 00:17:29.530
and took care of the Chicken Beast full-time,

00:17:29.930 --> 00:17:32.030
so of course I stopped earning income.

00:17:34.230 --> 00:17:37.800
Little by little, I sold off pieces 
of my land in order to make ends meet,

00:17:38.030 --> 00:17:40.800
until those three square meters 
were all that was left.

00:17:41.640 --> 00:17:45.840
So that's why you became attached 
to a wild Chicken Beast...

00:17:46.170 --> 00:17:50.350
But why are you trying to sell the 
last of that precious land now?

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:51.610
It's simple.

00:17:52.650 --> 00:17:55.450
I'm going to die soon.

00:17:57.820 --> 00:18:00.290
Old Man Yocchi, what do you 
mean, you're gonna die?!

00:18:01.720 --> 00:18:02.860
Don't be so surprised.

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:06.490
I can tell when I'm at the 
end of my road, at least.

00:18:06.960 --> 00:18:11.130
And so I decided to pass those 
three squared meters on to someone.

00:18:12.330 --> 00:18:16.740
By the way, Toriko, how much 
money did you bring with you?

00:18:16.970 --> 00:18:18.670
We've got a million.

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:21.380
Komatsu won the lottery.

00:18:21.480 --> 00:18:22.710
But, uh...

00:18:22.780 --> 00:18:24.450
A m-million?!

00:18:25.010 --> 00:18:29.080
Toriko-san, don't you 
have money in this case?!

00:18:29.720 --> 00:18:30.380
This is...

00:18:32.120 --> 00:18:34.920
...full of Stun Apples for him!

00:18:38.490 --> 00:18:39.790
Amusing!

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:41.430
Alright, sold!

00:18:41.930 --> 00:18:44.560
I'll let you boys have that piece of land.

00:18:45.430 --> 00:18:47.000
Seriously?!

00:18:47.330 --> 00:18:51.000
But wasn't the lowest bid ten billion?

00:18:51.400 --> 00:18:54.810
That's right. But that's only the 
price for the lowest of the low,

00:18:54.810 --> 00:18:57.080
who think of nothing but making money.

00:18:58.340 --> 00:19:01.150
So is that what you meant 
by "the lowest bid"?!

00:19:04.180 --> 00:19:07.820
Money holds no value to me now.

00:19:08.150 --> 00:19:11.490
With money, the more you 
stockpile, the less you have.

00:19:12.020 --> 00:19:13.830
To me, it loses value.

00:19:15.360 --> 00:19:16.100
Toriko...

00:19:18.360 --> 00:19:21.230
The words you said when 
you praised the egg...

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:25.070
It's mellow, but also with 
a strong, firm flavor!

00:19:26.170 --> 00:19:29.140
My wife said the same thing.

00:19:30.040 --> 00:19:32.980
It's mellow, yet has a strong, firm taste.

00:19:33.610 --> 00:19:35.350
This is so delicious...

00:19:36.210 --> 00:19:43.190
Those words... Those words are more 
valuable to me than anything...

00:19:44.220 --> 00:19:45.190
Old Man Yocchi...

00:19:46.420 --> 00:19:49.960
For giving me happiness, something 
that can never be bought with money...

00:19:49.960 --> 00:19:51.000
Thank you.

00:19:54.100 --> 00:19:58.740
I don't care how you use this land.

00:19:59.240 --> 00:20:00.140
There's just one thing.

00:20:00.570 --> 00:20:06.410
Meeko will get lonely after I'm gone, so 
will you play with her once in a while?

00:20:16.790 --> 00:20:19.660
Wow! A chick just hatched!

00:20:20.090 --> 00:20:22.090
Is it Old Man Yocchi reborn?

00:20:22.890 --> 00:20:25.760
Now they're together again, huh?

00:20:28.670 --> 00:20:31.370
We give thanks for this food, let's eat!

00:20:35.570 --> 00:20:37.210
Yuuuu... Toriko!

00:20:37.210 --> 00:20:39.940
Potassium, manganese, calcium, 
starch, fructose, and dextrose

00:20:39.940 --> 00:20:42.780
Magnesium, iron, vitamins ABCDE

00:20:42.780 --> 00:20:45.610
Vanadium, sodium, glucosamine, chondroitin

00:20:45.610 --> 00:20:48.480
Carotintintin, lycopenpenpene, 
isoflavonvonvone

00:20:48.480 --> 00:20:51.190
Celery, goya, and green peas

00:20:51.190 --> 00:20:54.020
Shiitake, liver, eggplant, bell pepper

00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:56.690
What a shame to say "I don't 
even want to look at them!"

00:20:56.690 --> 00:20:58.390
Even if you hate it, gobble 
it down 3 times or 4 times

00:20:58.390 --> 00:20:59.800
and it'll be more and more

00:20:59.800 --> 00:21:01.160
Yuuuu... Toriko!

00:21:01.160 --> 00:21:03.930
Eat 'em up more! Eat 'em up more!

00:21:03.930 --> 00:21:06.800
More and more and more and 
more and more! Eat 'em all up!

00:21:06.800 --> 00:21:11.070
Delicious things are delicious!  
Not even giving them a chance…

00:21:11.070 --> 00:21:12.410
Such a waste!

00:21:12.410 --> 00:21:15.240
Gobble 'em down more! Gobble 'em down more!

00:21:15.240 --> 00:21:18.050
Majorly, deeply, plentifully, 
heartily, gobble 'em down!

00:21:18.050 --> 00:21:23.650
They enrich your body and spirit! 
Be grateful to your meals today!

00:21:23.650 --> 00:21:26.550
Thanks for the food! All done!

00:21:29.060 --> 00:21:30.220
Dishing with Tina!

00:21:32.060 --> 00:21:34.260
It's "Dishing with Tina", the talk 
show with a heaping helping of fun!

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:38.770
Our guest today is that first-class 
gourmet architect, Smile-san.

00:21:39.530 --> 00:21:41.800
Known for designing the Gourmet 
Tower and the Gourmet Train,

00:21:39.530 --> 00:21:50.540
Smile - First-rate Gourmet Architect

00:21:41.900 --> 00:21:44.640
the brilliant architect Smile-san 
is in great demand these days.

00:21:44.840 --> 00:21:48.880
In fact, he's so busy sometimes 
that he forgets to smile, right?

00:21:49.010 --> 00:21:50.310
Even though he's Smile-san...

00:21:51.850 --> 00:21:54.850
Forget to smile? Who are you talking about?

00:21:55.750 --> 00:22:00.320
Oh! That smile doesn't even 
have a gram of gloominess!

00:22:00.990 --> 00:22:03.290
So how is work these days?

00:22:10.030 --> 00:22:14.970
As always, I've got a mountain 
of work orders. Thank you.

00:22:15.740 --> 00:22:17.300
What kind of job are you working on now?

00:22:17.800 --> 00:22:18.800
Um...

00:22:19.310 --> 00:22:22.580
Honestly, I'm blessed to have such 
a great deal of work to do...

00:22:23.240 --> 00:22:27.650
After this, I've got a meeting... 
then I go home and work at night...

00:22:28.650 --> 00:22:36.020
...'til... the sun... comes up...

00:22:37.020 --> 00:22:38.660
Hey... Smile-san!

00:22:42.030 --> 00:22:44.230
An aurora?! Is that...

00:22:45.200 --> 00:22:47.030
Century Soup...

00:22:47.770 --> 00:22:50.070
Komatsu-kun made me a special batch,

00:22:50.540 --> 00:22:54.210
and it's helped me keep a 
proper smile on my face...

00:22:55.640 --> 00:22:58.010
...but he needs to make it a little stronger.

00:22:59.310 --> 00:23:02.280
I don't believe this... You're 
addicted to Century Soup?!

00:23:02.810 --> 00:23:04.980
Let's go on to our next segment...

00:23:07.050 --> 00:23:09.090
Maximum difficulty! Maximum beauty!

00:23:09.550 --> 00:23:13.310
In pursuit of beautiful prey, set out with your new partner!

00:23:14.010 --> 00:23:16.690
Glittering Crystal! Shining Gourami!

00:23:17.360 --> 00:23:19.040
Look forward to another heaping helping of fun!
